---
// DRAFT — written to match how the software actually behaves, but it has not
// been reviewed by a solicitor. Before launch: confirm the company number and
// registered address, name the data processors you really use (Stripe, Google,
// your email provider, your host), and have someone qualified read it.
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../../lib/schema";

const crumbs = [
	{ label: "Home", href: "/" },
	{ label: "Privacy policy", href: "/legal/privacy/" },
];
const UPDATED = "31 July 2026";
---

<Page
	title="Privacy policy"
	description={`How ${SITE.company} handles personal data for ${SITE.name} — what the app sends, what the website collects, and who processes payments.`}
	intro={`Last updated ${UPDATED}. The short version: the app processes your video on your own computer, and we do not receive it.`}
	eyebrow="Legal"
	crumbs={crumbs}
	schema={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}
	cta={false}
	narrow
>
	<section class="pt-0">
		<div class="wrap wrap-narrow prose">
			<h2>Who we are</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE.name} is published by {SITE.company}, a company registered in
				{" "}{SITE.companyRegisteredIn} under company number {SITE.companyNumber}, with its
				registered office at {SITE.companyAddressLine}. That company is the data controller
				for everything described on this page.
			</p>
			<p>
				For any privacy question, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>What the desktop app sends</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Licence activation.</strong> Your licence key and an anonymous hardware
					fingerprint — a one-way hash of machine identifiers. It cannot be reversed into your
					name, your files or your hardware serial numbers, and its only purpose is enforcing
					one licence per computer.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Periodic licence checks.</strong> The same two values, occasionally, to
					confirm the licence is still valid.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Nothing else.</strong> No telemetry, no usage analytics, no crash uploads,
					no list of the videos you process.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>What the app sends to Google, on your behalf</h2>
			<p>
				AI features use <strong>your own</strong> Google Gemini API key, entered by you in
				Settings. Requests go directly from your computer to Google under your key, and are
				covered by your agreement with Google, not by us. Depending on the source video this
				can include the video's caption text, compressed audio for transcription, or — only in
				visual analysis mode, which you choose deliberately — a low-resolution copy of the
				video. We never see any of it.
			</p>
			<p>Your video file itself is never uploaded to us under any circumstances.</p>

			<h2>What the website collects</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Purchases.</strong> Card payments are handled by Stripe. We receive your
					email address, order details and country for tax purposes, but never see or store
					your card number. If you choose Pakistani bank or JazzCash payment, we receive
					your email, order reference, quoted amount, payment method, transaction ID and any
					optional payment screenshot you submit. Screenshots are stored privately and are
					used only to help verify, support or investigate that payment.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Email you send us.</strong> Kept as long as needed to support you, then deleted.</li>
				<li><strong>Advertising measurement.</strong> If advertising pixels are running, they may record that a visit or a purchase happened. This is disclosed in the cookie notice at the point it applies.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Referral tracking.</strong> If you arrive through an
					<a href="/affiliates/">affiliate link</a>, the affiliate's code — a short
					word such as <code>ali</code>, nothing about you — is stored in your
					browser for 60 days so that whoever recommended us is credited if you
					buy. It is passed to Stripe with a card purchase or attached to your
					pending bank-payment order. Clearing your browser's site data removes it, and
					nothing on the site behaves differently if it is not there.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Legal basis and retention</h2>
			<p>
				We process purchase data to perform the contract with you, and keep transaction records
				for as long as UK tax law requires. Licence records are kept for the life of the
				licence so it can be moved between machines and reissued if lost.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				Under UK GDPR you may request a copy of your data, ask for corrections, ask for
				deletion, or object to processing. Email us and we will respond within one month.
				Deleting your licence record ends your ability to reactivate or transfer the licence,
				so we will confirm before doing it.
			</p>

			<h2>Sharing</h2>
			<p>
				We do not sell personal data. It is shared only with the processors needed to run the
				business — payment, email and hosting providers — and only to the extent each needs.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes materially, the date at the top changes and the previous version
				is available on request.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Page>

<style>
	.pt-0 {
		padding-top: 8px;
	}
</style>
